  "executive_briefing": "As of September 2026, the digital asset regulatory landscape has experienced a major pivot following the U.S. Senate's failure to advance the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act past its cloture vote. This legislative setback has temporarily halted comprehensive federal safe harbors for non-custodial software developers, dampening the peak hype narrative around immediate regulatory integration. Meanwhile, institutional adoption of spot Bitcoin ETFs has faced a complex reality check with net outflows and slower momentum in the first half of 2026, transitioning the asset class into a disciplined operational and treasury phase. Despite legislative hurdles, developer interest remains firmly directed toward scaling native Bitcoin programmability and trust-minimized, intent-based cross-chain liquidity networks that bridge Bitcoin and EVM ecosystems without relying on vulnerable wrapped-asset bridges.",
